What this means
	•	Logic breakdown:
	•	633 ANDNOT → Big chunk of your logic simplifies into (a & ~b) type terms.
	•	310 MUX → Large multiplexer network → makes sense, your ALU has a case-switch on op. Each ALU op is selected via muxing.
	•	XOR (65) and XNOR (2) → Arithmetic and comparison (adders, SLT).
	•	OR (266), NOR (40), ORNOT (91) → Derived from bitwise OR and logic simplifications.
	•	NOT (31) → Inversions for control and arithmetic.
	•	NAND (64), AND (86) → Basic gates.
	•	Signals:
	•	1675 internal signals → intermediate wires.
	•	68 input signals → corresponds to your ALU ports (a[32], b[32], op[4]).
	•	32 + 32 + 4 = 68 ✔
	•	35 output signals → matches outputs (y[32] + 3 flags).
	•	32 + 3 = 35 ✔

👉 This confirms your netlist connectivity matches the RTL spec.

